# Vendored third-party source is copied byte-for-byte and compared byte-for-byte
# (tests/vendor-drift.test.ts). Git's autocrlf would rewrite line endings on
# checkout, so a Windows clone would hold 213-byte files where upstream ships
# 205-byte ones — the drift test would fail there and pass on Linux CI, and
# `scripts/copy-vendor.mjs` would publish whichever bytes the builder happened to
# have. `-text` turns the conversion off for this directory only.
src/vendor/** -text
